    "tree_id": "1b3577381d834d5c3de442b3c65bbebefd21f607",
    "message": "feat(mcp): express nullable inputs in MCP tool schemas (#9837) (#9843)\n\n* feat(mcp): express nullable inputs in MCP tool schemas (#9837)\n\nPublish \"may be null\" as standard JSON Schema `type: [<T>, \"null\"]`,\nauthored only through the branded `nullableProperty` builder. The\ntools/call validator accepts null only for nullable properties and keeps\ntype, enum, item and nested-object rules for non-null values. The catalog\nvalidator rejects a nullable confirmation binding. No descriptor adopts\nthe vocabulary; every published schema serializes byte-identically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(mcp): format nullable validation test (#9837)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mcp): keep cited mcp-contracts and mcp line ranges stable (#9837)\n\nAgent connector terms cite exact mcp-contracts.ts line ranges and the\nstatic-surface ledger cites mcp.ts:24-50. Drop the primitive-type\nrepublish and derive it locally in mcp.ts so no cited line moves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-17T10:12:00Z",
    "author": { "name": "Todd Skelton", "email": "todd.skelton@outlook.com" },
    "committer": { "name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com" }
  },
